From feb6e23bf9b38be3d4dbdc33f41032bf963ac993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:29:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 56/56] Demo page: the identity check says who enrolls and who
 checks, when the test face was enrolled, and its verdict in a result panel;
 the shorter subtitle (task 22)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two people each enrolled their own face and then checked it, so both
"passed"; the face check's "Good, face captured successfully" read as the
verdict, which was a small line under the buttons.

- Buttons: "1. Enroll the operator's face (once)", "2. Check identity
  (anyone)", "3. Delete test face"; the card says the operator enrolls once
  and anyone else is refused. Enrolling over an existing test face asks
  first ("Replace the enrolled test face?"); Cancel does not enroll.
- "Test face enrolled · today 13:16" (or its date), from a new Pigeon call,
  identityTestTemplateTime (the template file's lastModified, null when
  there is none; diagnostics builds only). hasIdentityTestTemplate stays for
  the debug page.
- The verdict is a result panel inside the card, like the check's result:
  "Same person" (green check), "Different person – refused" (red cross),
  the other outcomes neutral with their texts; "Similarity 0.82 · needed
  0.40" for every outcome with a number, MATCH included. After a check it
  scrolls into view. An enrolment or a delete is a short note, not a
  verdict, and clears the old verdict. Never an image.
- LivenessApi's "identity binding ..." log line ends with ", similarity
  0.82, threshold 0.40" in diagnostics builds (the score reaches Dart only
  there too); release builds log the outcome as before.
- Header subtitle: "Developer build · offline · no MOSIP server". It fits on
  one line, so the header's column now takes the full width (a column as
  wide as its longest line was centred).
- The reset question and the replace question share one dialog helper.

Tests: the identity flow (no question for a first enrolment, the enrolled
time, MATCH and NO_MATCH with icon, colour and numbers, delete); the replace
question and its Cancel; every outcome in the panel at 360x640 and 1.3
(sentence, icon, colour, numbers or none, no image, no overflow), and a
face check not passed; the panel scrolls into view; the overflow checks
also cover a refusal and the replace question, and that the header starts
at the gutter. flutter test test/liveness: 302 passing, 20 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
